[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-11754"] :question/worked-solution "From the diagram we see that the arms of the parabola open to the right. The parabola has its vertex at $(0,0)$ and passes through the point $(12,4).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(0,0)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSince we know the given parabola passes through the point $(12,4),$ we can substitute $x=12$ and $y=4$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {4}^{2} & =4p(12) \\\\ 16 & =48p \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(\\frac{1}{3})x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =\\frac{4}{3}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the arms of the parabola open to the right since $p=\\frac{1}{3}$ is positive." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-11762/selection/bc159fa037ddd299186fbb2d8f6c509131b7677bdd73e951522e3373f16a83a9" :answer/id #uuid "36e5bfb1-e509-5844-816a-af325a539188" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=6x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11762/selection/e2ac2577bc1511d2fb55bb11f333d5433ab3d6a316b25257932f20b05c7c49e3" :answer/id #uuid "c44b7aee-a618-5989-8e93-dead09c18b2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=3x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11762/selection/5464b6528434685d90a63424ddd11c4edd590ea7e9ed4845e0656c30ab8dba3b" :answer/id #uuid "bc5407e0-fb8a-5cfb-95c0-88d83a5655f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-3x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11762/selection/d364a8f4952113723a80a93957107ad5ce79e5147e7a3766085659e6da22fe39" :answer/id #uuid "7cda709d-4b28-522b-8263-8d55e6f88209" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11762/selection/f7e2b4506bb6c8f1b5f22b9d8f12146b7c8411c18c9e10eb470616ac3abd122b" :answer/id #uuid "6e6dbc94-be06-5a41-8111-7295ce983a9e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-6x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11762/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8536da56-fd61-54fe-8645-fa489e812420" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-11762/selection/f7e2b4506bb6c8f1b5f22b9d8f12146b7c8411c18c9e10eb470616ac3abd122b" :answer-field/choices ["q-11762/selection/bc159fa037ddd299186fbb2d8f6c509131b7677bdd73e951522e3373f16a83a9" "q-11762/selection/e2ac2577bc1511d2fb55bb11f333d5433ab3d6a316b25257932f20b05c7c49e3" "q-11762/selection/5464b6528434685d90a63424ddd11c4edd590ea7e9ed4845e0656c30ab8dba3b" "q-11762/selection/d364a8f4952113723a80a93957107ad5ce79e5147e7a3766085659e6da22fe39" "q-11762/selection/f7e2b4506bb6c8f1b5f22b9d8f12146b7c8411c18c9e10eb470616ac3abd122b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-11762" :question/id #uuid "ac2ca03d-2104-57cd-88e6-485cf3ecb522" :question/math-academy-id "q-11762" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13954664/assets/a2f289efe5b8f44c27b5d1ffe6d46d58a658f7f81155736288bc621909dd7727.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram we see that the arms of the parabola open to the left. The parabola has its vertex at $(0,0)$ and passes through the point $(-6,6).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(0,0)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSince we know the given parabola passes through the point $(-6,6),$ we can substitute $x=-6$ and $y=6$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {6}^{2} & =4p(-6) \\\\ 36 & =-24p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(-\\frac{3}{2})x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-6x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the arms of the parabola open to the left since $p=-\\frac{3}{2}$ is negative." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-11762/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "75fd35db-6b4e-5820-b6ac-925d24a0f117"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11762"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-11756/selection/6db1b3e26b30525d4ed7a09400dccbe999a5c2e2b1954ea0dec60d75c907de2c" :answer/id #uuid "a88f675d-6840-581f-9c5c-03e6fe6c00cc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=2x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11756/selection/d364a8f4952113723a80a93957107ad5ce79e5147e7a3766085659e6da22fe39" :answer/id #uuid "4bedc011-7d43-573d-8c67-e31f92bc18fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11756/selection/5464b6528434685d90a63424ddd11c4edd590ea7e9ed4845e0656c30ab8dba3b" :answer/id #uuid "6ab794d0-acb9-590a-b9e6-a7e41f2578fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-3x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11756/selection/4e8641b3cb277b07635b8e62ec1c6e93dad5212e3307ba76c4f4f45915fe36b6" :answer/id #uuid "957d01a4-bd8b-5bb5-a4fe-0ea865bc7119" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11756/selection/de0b677261bde629b5e156f8561b705314fbfb38516123f6ed9161ad8add8643" :answer/id #uuid "4226fcb3-36d4-5b40-bcf7-9acf6f5a7b91" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-2x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11756/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "37620f75-70e3-5e0e-9ebd-5024d4622914" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-11756/selection/d364a8f4952113723a80a93957107ad5ce79e5147e7a3766085659e6da22fe39" :answer-field/choices ["q-11756/selection/6db1b3e26b30525d4ed7a09400dccbe999a5c2e2b1954ea0dec60d75c907de2c" "q-11756/selection/d364a8f4952113723a80a93957107ad5ce79e5147e7a3766085659e6da22fe39" "q-11756/selection/5464b6528434685d90a63424ddd11c4edd590ea7e9ed4845e0656c30ab8dba3b" "q-11756/selection/4e8641b3cb277b07635b8e62ec1c6e93dad5212e3307ba76c4f4f45915fe36b6" "q-11756/selection/de0b677261bde629b5e156f8561b705314fbfb38516123f6ed9161ad8add8643"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-11756" :question/id #uuid "60215e1f-40ad-54ae-b2a1-1986343ee299" :question/math-academy-id "q-11756" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13954664/assets/58c92cc542f027ec882191d2b4631f9fcf3704820b2825a18f30dbdc3f59d07b.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram we see that the arms of the parabola open to the left. The parabola has its vertex at $(0,0)$ and passes through the point $(-4,2).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(0,0)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSince we know the given parabola passes through the point $(-4,2),$ we can substitute $x=-4$ and $y=2$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {2}^{2} & =4p(-4) \\\\ 4 & =-16p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(-\\frac{1}{4})x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the arms of the parabola open to the left since $p=-\\frac{1}{4}$ is negative." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-11756/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "75fd35db-6b4e-5820-b6ac-925d24a0f117"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11756"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115625/selection/860826249f63e2e710924ee61bfe13806e1c2de2c49ecf55879bf018a65fddf0" :answer/id #uuid "e257f06d-b2af-57e0-974c-daae06b1d9f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-\\frac{1}{4}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115625/selection/0a8eeb5fd7cf4ecec2547e82e37d28aada07ac627505caa80b41e59c53cbd5e1" :answer/id #uuid "67bbc023-ac58-5171-908d-2badfbe1d3a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=4x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115625/selection/51f9c0e0b28c4d7e7ad94829c69c4ff4c5b96efc242224c78146ef16ecfebbc0" :answer/id #uuid "ff3afbb8-119f-511b-a599-963062379f97" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=\\frac{1}{4}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115625/selection/4e8641b3cb277b07635b8e62ec1c6e93dad5212e3307ba76c4f4f45915fe36b6" :answer/id #uuid "63d16d93-ebd9-50d6-8243-2b7d9b616fa3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115625/selection/d364a8f4952113723a80a93957107ad5ce79e5147e7a3766085659e6da22fe39" :answer/id #uuid "b0cefe60-f116-5701-8d83-433ca3e0b8f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115625/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a0ccf9bd-7fb1-568b-ad99-4cfc3bfd80ec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115625/selection/d364a8f4952113723a80a93957107ad5ce79e5147e7a3766085659e6da22fe39" :answer-field/choices ["q-115625/selection/860826249f63e2e710924ee61bfe13806e1c2de2c49ecf55879bf018a65fddf0" "q-115625/selection/0a8eeb5fd7cf4ecec2547e82e37d28aada07ac627505caa80b41e59c53cbd5e1" "q-115625/selection/51f9c0e0b28c4d7e7ad94829c69c4ff4c5b96efc242224c78146ef16ecfebbc0" "q-115625/selection/4e8641b3cb277b07635b8e62ec1c6e93dad5212e3307ba76c4f4f45915fe36b6" "q-115625/selection/d364a8f4952113723a80a93957107ad5ce79e5147e7a3766085659e6da22fe39"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115625" :question/id #uuid "1dea1f83-fad7-5576-8d47-906556eb6e45" :question/math-academy-id "q-115625" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13954664/assets/b14a6063e0b1be751e738060087644cacaa3c3cf1e324ee66bf57232834e618d.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram we see that the arms of the parabola open to the left. The parabola has its vertex at $(0,0)$ and passes through the point $(-1,1).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(0,0)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSince we know the given parabola passes through the point $(-1,1),$ we can substitute $x=-1$ and $y=1$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {1}^{2} & =4p(-1) \\\\ 1 & =-4p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(-\\frac{1}{4})x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the arms of the parabola open to the left since $p=-\\frac{1}{4}$ is negative." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-115625/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "75fd35db-6b4e-5820-b6ac-925d24a0f117"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115625"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-11766/selection/987ad0acd4f9e1ebd05cb3b1d7a920a7def8be2e463a221c31ac9760b5a01e53" :answer/id #uuid "70033e47-9f97-595f-a286-665e0a675967" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=\\frac{8}{3}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11766/selection/519869be4e703d7740ced8ba548b0010575f08320ebae9d37de1183442594b3a" :answer/id #uuid "545ed32a-9620-53a3-803e-05e95feec346" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=\\frac{16}{3}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11766/selection/0bdd16609d5a9f5d7b5c53397896355b31e1243c0f9ec77f16695e0e1d44cc11" :answer/id #uuid "59a79825-0048-5374-871a-337913530b02" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-\\frac{8}{3}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11766/selection/dfbc1d59a03687f9864620c40e1e41a051269868505c373916416e7fc47a73b8" :answer/id #uuid "2085197b-65ca-5569-836d-47dd79c382f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-\\frac{4}{3}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11766/selection/44f4bdc30964627fed35209feaf62bf44871a1fc764c810cb7acd481968efc90" :answer/id #uuid "37bc927a-5eb2-59a3-ab19-31ab8759ae55" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-\\frac{16}{3}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11766/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2897e241-7063-5da3-a9b0-7744ca11dc3a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-11766/selection/44f4bdc30964627fed35209feaf62bf44871a1fc764c810cb7acd481968efc90" :answer-field/choices ["q-11766/selection/987ad0acd4f9e1ebd05cb3b1d7a920a7def8be2e463a221c31ac9760b5a01e53" "q-11766/selection/519869be4e703d7740ced8ba548b0010575f08320ebae9d37de1183442594b3a" "q-11766/selection/0bdd16609d5a9f5d7b5c53397896355b31e1243c0f9ec77f16695e0e1d44cc11" "q-11766/selection/dfbc1d59a03687f9864620c40e1e41a051269868505c373916416e7fc47a73b8" "q-11766/selection/44f4bdc30964627fed35209feaf62bf44871a1fc764c810cb7acd481968efc90"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-11766" :question/id #uuid "cf8c8267-197c-5fa6-a8cf-451234107143" :question/math-academy-id "q-11766" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13954664/assets/6723e1c76d63216151e7c78d67c882ae98f9af950675e37ced726e8ce5aea4d3.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram we see that the arms of the parabola open to the left. The parabola has its vertex at $(0,0)$ and passes through the point $(-12,8).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(0,0)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSince we know the given parabola passes through the point $(-12,8),$ we can substitute $x=-12$ and $y=8$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {8}^{2} & =4p(-12) \\\\ 64 & =-48p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(-\\frac{4}{3})x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-\\frac{16}{3}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the arms of the parabola open to the left since $p=-\\frac{4}{3}$ is negative." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-11766/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "75fd35db-6b4e-5820-b6ac-925d24a0f117"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11766"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-11763"] :question/worked-solution "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(0,0)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSince we know the given parabola passes through the point $(-12,6),$ we can substitute $x=-12$ and $y=6$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {6}^{2} & =4p(-12) \\\\ 36 & =-48p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(-\\frac{3}{4})x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-3x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-115634/selection/cd26ced14f629c06f52fd7e533ddb774a03d32d9589d327718a0cba9a749435b" :answer/id #uuid "af22acc3-5ff2-59da-8d01-efaca6071df3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-\\frac{1}{16}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115634/selection/9dfcfe12c244434cfb49a5e16208ecbf8af2ae4a0cdc37c87d6e245a90ced56c" :answer/id #uuid "32cc0167-455d-558a-9fbc-a2bfaf637780" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-16x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115634/selection/7a35be791bf0edec1186bc37