lve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ (-4)^{2} & =4p(-1) \\\\ 16 & =-4p \\\\ p & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(-4)x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-16x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-115634/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "17099881-d7b9-54d9-a29a-4f5f28561cd3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115634"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115631/selection/9dfcfe12c244434cfb49a5e16208ecbf8af2ae4a0cdc37c87d6e245a90ced56c" :answer/id #uuid "38e7bf11-4c43-55d5-9f7a-637bdbf27ae4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-16x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115631/selection/6db1b3e26b30525d4ed7a09400dccbe999a5c2e2b1954ea0dec60d75c907de2c" :answer/id #uuid "df0c7e8f-120b-51df-9fcb-2fe4352cea5b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=2x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115631/selection/9ed799ac9bbeb1220129ebe93cc085fdc971782473cceadd0f1673fa053740e6" :answer/id #uuid "13a8146a-a778-5a19-9a8d-732040bc9426" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}=2y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115631/selection/7a35be791bf0edec1186bc37a1baffbcfb47911c6487d7c1c870d96ec786ab49" :answer/id #uuid "b5186bb9-878d-5662-845c-aec58d799d7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{2}=4y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115631/selection/3d2070a91b3f93e2ff3f01bbf9bffb1b6bac79b45237069ea1f5092d2b29dd3c" :answer/id #uuid "738f6646-2b0e-54a7-a66f-3f88a8fb5332" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=\\frac{1}{2}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115631/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3cdc193e-5221-50b3-b374-abfd779910bd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115631/selection/6db1b3e26b30525d4ed7a09400dccbe999a5c2e2b1954ea0dec60d75c907de2c" :answer-field/choices ["q-115631/selection/9dfcfe12c244434cfb49a5e16208ecbf8af2ae4a0cdc37c87d6e245a90ced56c" "q-115631/selection/6db1b3e26b30525d4ed7a09400dccbe999a5c2e2b1954ea0dec60d75c907de2c" "q-115631/selection/9ed799ac9bbeb1220129ebe93cc085fdc971782473cceadd0f1673fa053740e6" "q-115631/selection/7a35be791bf0edec1186bc37a1baffbcfb47911c6487d7c1c870d96ec786ab49" "q-115631/selection/3d2070a91b3f93e2ff3f01bbf9bffb1b6bac79b45237069ea1f5092d2b29dd3c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115631" :question/id #uuid "03ff4c40-b67c-529b-8313-05d8daa83019" :question/math-academy-id "q-115631" :question/problem "Find the equation of the right-opening parabola that has its vertex at  $(0,0)$ and passes through the point $(8,-4).$" :question/worked-solution "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(0,0)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSince we know the given parabola passes through the point $(8,-4),$ we can substitute $x=8$ and $y=-4$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ (-4)^{2} & =4p(8) \\\\ 16 & =32p \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(\\frac{1}{2})x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-115631/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "17099881-d7b9-54d9-a29a-4f5f28561cd3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115631"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-11751/selection/7a51c7b41e0faa12691fd9ae585e993d25d73d9e1ff7e456dc3ad6d9744e0710" :answer/id #uuid "edb3077d-eeda-5dc3-b79c-f796b335c13e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-8x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11751/selection/bc159fa037ddd299186fbb2d8f6c509131b7677bdd73e951522e3373f16a83a9" :answer/id #uuid "75105eb6-