\n$$\n\nSince we know the given parabola passes through the point $(-8,8),$ we can substitute $x=-8$ and $y=8$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {8}^{2} & =4p(-8) \\\\ 64 & =-32p \\\\ p & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(-2)x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-8x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-11751/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "17099881-d7b9-54d9-a29a-4f5f28561cd3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11751"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-11757/selection/44f4bdc30964627fed35209feaf62bf44871a1fc764c810cb7acd481968efc90" :answer/id #uuid "2749846f-ba01-5229-b433-624512db0aaf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-\\frac{16}{3}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11757/selection/0bdd16609d5a9f5d7b5c53397896355b31e1243c0f9ec77f16695e0e1d44cc11" :answer/id #uuid "033224ba-3b4c-5bed-8ccc-9b34855442cf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-\\frac{8}{3}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11757/selection/987ad0acd4f9e1ebd05cb3b1d7a920a7def8be2e463a221c31ac9760b5a01e53" :answer/id #uuid "aec062f0-2dbd-5eb0-9341-c573aaeca55c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=\\frac{8}{3}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11757/selection/dfbc1d59a03687f9864620c40e1e41a051269868505c373916416e7fc47a73b8" :answer/id #uuid "cbdef78f-8bc9-5385-8bb2-1d6a7e36e5d6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-\\frac{4}{3}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11757/selection/2381990babb18cc615a66c62495f1fd7c6db6b5da4727049dc6dc0bd8583a5be" :answer/id #uuid "cc1e5fc7-988e-577b-a6d4-07423d4ed819" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=\\frac{4}{3}x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11757/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fef4c39e-ea29-5165-8291-137d4b572f62" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-11757/selection/0bdd16609d5a9f5d7b5c53397896355b31e1243c0f9ec77f16695e0e1d44cc11" :answer-field/choices ["q-11757/selection/44f4bdc30964627fed35209feaf62bf44871a1fc764c810cb7acd481968efc90" "q-11757/selection/0bdd16609d5a9f5d7b5c53397896355b31e1243c0f9ec77f16695e0e1d44cc11" "q-11757/selection/987ad0acd4f9e1ebd05cb3b1d7a920a7def8be2e463a221c31ac9760b5a01e53" "q-11757/selection/dfbc1d59a03687f9864620c40e1e41a051269868505c373916416e7fc47a73b8" "q-11757/selection/2381990babb18cc615a66c62495f1fd7c6db6b5da4727049dc6dc0bd8583a5be"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-11757" :question/id #uuid "07838d7d-bdf0-550d-9b73-045741b48872" :question/math-academy-id "q-11757" :question/problem "Find the equation of the left-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ and passes through the point $(-6,-4).$" :question/worked-solution "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(0,0)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n{y}^{2}=4px.\n$$\n\nSince we know the given parabola passes through the point $(-6,-4),$ we can substitute $x=-6$ and $y=-4$ into the standard equation and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ (-4)^{2} & =4p(-6) \\\\ 16 & =-24p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4px \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(-\\frac{2}{3})x \\\\ {y}^{2} & =-\\frac{8}{3}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-11757/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "17099881-d7b9-54d9-a29a-4f5f28561cd3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11757"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115636/selection/214ec62b63cbb138a97ad7853c78ec5b5f7b939fc844dd898e6bfc960d144f0a" :answer/id #uuid "f3c221b2-f5fd-5ae3-9900-0df1a3001953" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+1)^{2}=-\\frac{9}{8}(x+2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115636/selection/24b9705768a55fbf3cecaa5d787dfc8b1177847e808159bd6e2a5a7d5b797806" :answer/id #uuid "464d585e-eab0-5ca3-b44a-1124e142c210" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}=\\frac{9}{8}(y+2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115636/selection/b5de5a525fda15b823214bb10f5cd586c33f78dab46b0739ce18724981c6e73f" :answer/id #uuid "37bf17eb-fa70-5cff-895a-07a5b3ebc5af" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+2)^{2}=\\frac{9}{2}(x+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115636/selection/1341f90cb900aaa52be842465ef63f3cfb26325f3354d827820553740554dc6f" :answer/id #uuid "08b73b54-8b69-5a59-896f-d8073bfad50c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+1)^{2}=-\\frac{9}{2}(x+2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115636/selection/529e84b4f7a60a565201635323ee32b8941a27985880874a765aa13be452d180" :answer/id #uuid "a834de73-80d7-532c-82a6-bb45b080ba37" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y-1)^{2}=\\frac{9}{8}(x-2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115636/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "56e190e5-5c3d-57f2-84d5-74194fc76dd0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115636/selection/1341f90cb900aaa52be842465ef63f3cfb26325f3354d827820553740554dc6f" :answer-field/choices ["q-115636/selection/214ec62b63cbb138a97ad7853c78ec5b5f7b939fc844dd898e6bfc960d144f0a" "q-115636/selection/24b9705768a55fbf3cecaa5d787dfc8b1177847e808159bd6e2a5a7d5b797806" "q-115636/selection/b5de5a525fda15b823214bb10f5cd586c33f78dab46b0739ce18724981c6e73f" "q-115636/selection/1341f90cb900aaa52be842465ef63f3cfb26325f3354d827820553740554dc6f" "q-115636/selection/529e84b4f7a60a565201635323ee32b8941a27985880874a765aa13be452d180"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115636" :question/id #uuid "4a6e5633-dfb8-5833-aa29-5b1d91e7af29" :question/math-academy-id "q-115636" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13954664/assets/5742f3f1161782d06b8a785d28d6c59b1e40aec37bd6b62268d6d41e1c662ee0.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram we see that the arms of the parabola open to the left. The parabola has its vertex at $(-2,-1)$ and passes through the point $(-4,-4).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(h,k)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-k)^{2} & =4p(x-h).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the given parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(-2,-1),$ we substitute $h=-2$ and $k=-1$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+1)^{2} & =4p(x+2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that the given parabola passes through the point $(-4,-4),$ so we can substitute $x=-4$ and $y=-4$ into the equation above and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+1)^{2} & =4p(x+2) \\\\ (-4+1)^{2} & =4p(-4+2) \\\\ 9 & =-8p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{9}{8}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+1)^{2} & =4p(x+2) \\\\ (y+1)^{2} & =4(-\\frac{9}{8})(x+2) \\\\ (y+1)^{2} & =-\\frac{9}{2}(x+2).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the arms of the parabola open to the left since $p=-\\frac{9}{8}$ is negative." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-115636/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc86c375-c2c4-56b7-a207-0abfc9709f6a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115636"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-11805/selection/cd13836d3356c3edab9bba6a62f71feaf4ec3731de0858b93b41a9e15e8558e0" :answer/id #uuid "2609fed3-abe9-5a2c-b07f-e531745d05c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-2(x+4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11805/selection/bc37d71e4fe3415cde66c67670c917a7946a707c2e4735557e42ecfe3556e62b" :answer/id #uuid "9fac91c2-60ab-5a3e-a44c-9441fd351a77" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=2(x+4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11805/selection/6bf74e1168c431c4ccf273f58d03a4ce4cbc6f97ed8161099642e1a81d2f3a16" :answer/id #uuid "2886ed4e-f111-54a9-a561-4954119104ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=-3(x+4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11805/selection/54b1d49e4fd7e0e069c2f2da5809a0a8cc71839602ca73b978612af3127ae454" :answer/id #uuid "6be78b89-a2b1-5c49-b541-44622f7e9839" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{y}^{2}=3(x+4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11805/selection/7c6379bef02f1664f7473052c3e87780f132beab9ce9bb909223bf41d58999ff" :answer/id #uuid "30773eb0-8e48-5ff6-9988-d2aebb7ef7a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+4)^{2}=3x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11805/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8ea9ebdb-5005-5c15-a63d-c09c01cce912" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-11805/selection/54b1d49e4fd7e0e069c2f2da5809a0a8cc71839602ca73b978612af3127ae454" :answer-field/choices ["q-11805/selection/cd13836d3356c3edab9bba6a62f71feaf4ec3731de0858b93b41a9e15e8558e0" "q-11805/selection/bc37d71e4fe3415cde66c67670c917a7946a707c2e4735557e42ecfe3556e62b" "q-11805/selection/6bf74e1168c431c4ccf273f58d03a4ce4cbc6f97ed8161099642e1a81d2f3a16" "q-11805/selection/54b1d49e4fd7e0e069c2f2da5809a0a8cc71839602ca73b978612af3127ae454" "q-11805/selection/7c6379bef02f1664f7473052c3e87780f132beab9ce9bb909223bf41d58999ff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-11805" :question/id #uuid "51fd9c57-bec5-5968-83e1-20a46bdee323" :question/math-academy-id "q-11805" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13954664/assets/a16f3f2ba78b5aef180c4331d1dd99f37340d2c6d842c1596e35445f1dbf34c5.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram we see that the arms of the parabola open to the right. The parabola has its vertex at $(-4,0)$ and passes through the point $(8,6).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(h,k)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-k)^{2} & =4p(x-h).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the given parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(-4,0),$ we substitute $h=-4$ and $k=0$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4p(x+4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that the given parabola passes through the point $(8,6),$ so we can substitute $x=8$ and $y=6$ into the equation above and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4p(x+4) \\\\ {6}^{2} & =4p(8+4) \\\\ 36 & =48p \\\\ p & =\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2} & =4p(x+4) \\\\ {y}^{2} & =4(\\frac{3}{4})(x+4) \\\\ {y}^{2} & =3(x+4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the arms of the parabola open to the right since $p=\\frac{3}{4}$ is positive." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-11805/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc86c375-c2c4-56b7-a207-0abfc9709f6a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11805"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115640/selection/bc23e884d849e07014c988e762593cf3dc3a9690c17112f01a160f476bbe2c20" :answer/id #uuid "6faf3cff-1208-501c-bd13-4ddc53d72dba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x-3)^{2}=-12(y-3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115640/selection/0ded5ce97ee27a011fcfd26f9c82c4918c9fcee8b6a57f43acc86b691454784c" :answer/id #uuid "01480733-3dea-5b7a-a998-8e6987364ac0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+3)^{2}=3(x+3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115640/selection/0579ea3259ae0558315ae0e77b23961fac9ba02abb2b704d0389b54acbf278a5" :answer/id #uuid "2a282ecd-9120-5164-9142-e8fed956f6fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y-3)^{2}=-\\frac{3}{8}(x-3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115640/selection/466e6cf6d863e044c1e14c2bc23c1409ab00550135f3b502b387519278872c02" :answer/id #uuid "90da7ecc-92e5-566f-b1ae-aa71cd79d6d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+3)^{2}=\\frac{3}{2}(x+3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115640/selection/d50e341b30ceafb26fc17815210bc9125fd01fc8e9a05ba454476291a04cc400" :answer/id #uuid "3a407151-85b6-55e5-94c1-77ac3be02ee1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y-3)^{2}=12(x-3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115640/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "094bad5d-3056-51a0-b6a9-d51a378c2415" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115640/selection/d50e341b30ceafb26fc17815210bc9125fd01fc8e9a05ba454476291a04cc400" :answer-field/choices ["q-115640/selection/bc23e884d849e07014c988e762593cf3dc3a9690c17112f01a160f476bbe2c20" "q-115640/selection/0ded5ce97ee27a011fcfd26f9c82c4918c9fcee8b6a57f43acc86b691454784c" "q-115640/selection/0579ea3259ae0558315ae0e77b23961fac9ba02abb2b704d0389b54acbf278a5" "q-115640/selection/466e6cf6d863e044c1e14c2bc23c1409ab00550135f3b502b387519278872c02" "q-115640/selection/d50e341b30ceafb26fc17815210bc9125fd01fc8e9a05ba454476291a04cc400"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115640" :question/id #uuid "a7d690cd-8b12-547d-a0c5-09b9dbca554a" :question/math-academy-id "q-115640" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13954664/assets/c88e54f2a7acec3815a53fa4b0d641dd370ccf708b876f8dd231f05e115ea6fc.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram we see that the arms of the parabola open to the right. The parabola has its vertex at $(3,3)$ and passes through the point $(6,-3).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(h,k)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-k)^{2} & =4p(x-h).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the given parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(3,3),$ we substitute $h=3$ and $k=3$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-3)^{2} & =4p(x-3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that the given parabola passes through the point $(6,-3),$ so we can substitute $x=6$ and $y=-3$ into the equation above and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-3)^{2} & =4p(x-3) \\\\ (-3-3)^{2} & =4p(6-3) \\\\ 36 & =12p \\\\ p & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-3)^{2} & =4p(x-3) \\\\ (y-3)^{2} & =4(3)(x-3) \\\\ (y-3)^{2} & =12(x-3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the arms of the parabola open to the right since $p=3$ is positive." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-115640/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc86c375-c2c4-56b7-a207-0abfc9709f6a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115640"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115642/selection/fef5c1da04c781d7a22732fe2fca6c634ae0ff2fd09ad52a3844a2e2503ccfab" :answer/id #uuid "ad19b9f2-055b-586b-9a5d-e77023716b64" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}=-\\frac{1}{3}(y+2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115642/selection/2876410610e13cf4d389a817dcaa392488f5dec357699bca0681ab45f35d0a8d" :answer/id #uuid "cbcedba0-8ff8-5837-8b42-1222a6271b0f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+2)^{2}=\\frac{1}{3}(x-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115642/selection/060a642290d73ae9de06893162a50354a6b6cab6f2f2aa492016a121ea113629" :answer/id #uuid "1456629a-632f-5ab9-bcaa-2d15e43785b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y-2)^{2}=\\frac{1}{12}(x+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115642/selection/e2351fea591e07d10c804763a33df3b2393c24fbc1baa9a2915d0c6826c998b0" :answer/id #uuid "92049e69-d2e7-5684-b6a2-06013facd85d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+2)^{2}=-\\frac{9}{4}(x-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115642/selection/c536f51d13ea63542f29f9bc517e4fb0dca1912dcbd768f810ed1b48e50f9acc" :answer/id #uuid "858e2d4d-13e4-5f65-8f2f-6978a41bbf4b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+2)^{2}=9(x-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115642/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e4d32c64-ecfc-56c6-b87e-29cad4634755" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115642/selection/2876410610e13cf4d389a817dcaa392488f5dec357699bca0681ab45f35d0a8d" :answer-field/choices ["q-115642/selection/fef5c1da04c781d7a22732fe2fca6c634ae0ff2fd09ad52a3844a2e2503ccfab" "q-115642/selection/2876410610e13cf4d389a817dcaa392488f5dec357699bca0681ab45f35d0a8d" "q-115642/selection/060a642290d73ae9de06893162a50354a6b6cab6f2f2aa492016a121ea113629" "q-115642/selection/e2351fea591e07d10c804763a33df3b2393c24fbc1baa9a2915d0c6826c998b0" "q-115642/selection/c536f51d13ea63542f29f9bc517e4fb0dca1912dcbd768f810ed1b48e50f9acc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115642" :question/id #uuid "095475ac-3d42-523d-8b3e-46287aade654" :question/math-academy-id "q-115642" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13954664/assets/8ea1ad85f30978bed681f48e02f4af2f401a1f561390bee09683ead252fc1d7d.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram we see that the arms of the parabola open to the right. The parabola has its vertex at $(1,-2)$ and passes through the point $(4,-3).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(h,k)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-k)^{2} & =4p(x-h).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the given parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(1,-2),$ we substitute $h=1$ and $k=-2$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+2)^{2} & =4p(x-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that the given parabola passes through the point $(4,-3),$ so we can substitute $x=4$ and $y=-3$ into the equation above and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+2)^{2} & =4p(x-1) \\\\ (-3+2)^{2} & =4p(4-1) \\\\ 1 & =12p \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+2)^{2} & =4p(x-1) \\\\ (y+2)^{2} & =4(\\frac{1}{12})(x-1) \\\\ (y+2)^{2} & =\\frac{1}{3}(x-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the arms of the parabola open to the right since $p=\\frac{1}{12}$ is positive." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-115642/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc86c375-c2c4-56b7-a207-0abfc9709f6a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115642"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-11801/selection/5c2b1743078ecfd16f16f2f0fb293701a53b6cd08ad6d5fa00b83064f9dae966" :answer/id #uuid "493960ae-7ea2-5e9b-8c58-d86b9b5c73f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y-2)^{2}=\\frac{16}{3}(x+4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11801/selection/2e2f02f72260cc19588960c449d9148c87d8420fd2e0014b9391c5181ce70db8" :answer/id #uuid "33733aa8-212d-5f32-a63f-91b041cb378b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y-2)^{2}=-\\frac{16}{3}(x+4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11801/selection/43851fc3a6f0b10bac9dd9d0476dfdef21da0043a60fbb2a7650fa554f176971" :answer/id #uuid "04c925b0-049b-57fb-a247-a4722706fe2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+4)^{2}=\\frac{8}{3}(x-2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11801/selection/38a840c143e0c10a80cc8f2070b13dec86ef8bd76a203328991bf1090aafc0d9" :answer/id #uuid "9407e25c-2e28-53b6-b11e-b1068072c9a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y-2)^{2}=-\\frac{8}{3}(x+4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11801/selection/e8aeef8e0bd660a10b6d743bda9d0a5b4df161f563ca6d849864a2b11e18143d" :answer/id #uuid "53b22762-caa2-59a8-b6de-07319cdb4ee6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y-2)^{2}=\\frac{8}{3}(x+4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11801/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "51ef251d-e219-59a5-99c2-74aa9433e793" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-11801/selection/e8aeef8e0bd660a10b6d743bda9d0a5b4df161f563ca6d849864a2b11e18143d" :answer-field/choices ["q-11801/selection/5c2b1743078ecfd16f16f2f0fb293701a53b6cd08ad6d5fa00b83064f9dae966" "q-11801/selection/2e2f02f72260cc19588960c449d9148c87d8420fd2e0014b9391c5181ce70db8" "q-11801/selection/43851fc3a6f0b10bac9dd9d0476dfdef21da0043a60fbb2a7650fa554f176971" "q-11801/selection/38a840c143e0c10a80cc8f2070b13dec86ef8bd76a203328991bf1090aafc0d9" "q-11801/selection/e8aeef8e0bd660a10b6d743bda9d0a5b4df161f563ca6d849864a2b11e18143d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-11801" :question/id #uuid "7f36f5b9-9ac8-5800-8107-0386a4361e15" :question/math-academy-id "q-11801" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13954664/assets/d4d0ad25fe8409b55ad4021c5e06d0f13579cea804b1a2b78b18b3ba76bd0c0e.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the parabola shown above?" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram we see that the arms of the parabola open to the right. The parabola has its vertex at $(-4,2)$ and passes through the point $(2,6).$\n\nThe general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(h,k)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-k)^{2} & =4p(x-h).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the given parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(-4,2),$ we substitute $h=-4$ and $k=2$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-2)^{2} & =4p(x+4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that the given parabola passes through the point $(2,6),$ so we can substitute $x=2$ and $y=6$ into the equation above and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-2)^{2} & =4p(x+4) \\\\ (6-2)^{2} & =4p(2+4) \\\\ 16 & =24p \\\\ p & =\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-2)^{2} & =4p(x+4) \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =4(\\frac{2}{3})(x+4) \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =\\frac{8}{3}(x+4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the arms of the parabola open to the right since $p=\\frac{2}{3}$ is positive." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-11801/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dc86c375-c2c4-56b7-a207-0abfc9709f6a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11801"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-11794/selection/744273781c0ebbac96544b9ea3174f01adea99be43eb05bcf13825a7e5f9db87" :answer/id #uuid "7839009f-cb3b-561b-87c2-05a125ad1ada" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y-4)^{2}=-4(x-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11794/selection/5ea92dcac1f699d65c82b57d915fc42a88835c79e6b904d4ea8c316401c9c0f9" :answer/id #uuid "316676c5-b207-5ca0-8eb7-7e127d6a4655" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y-4)^{2}=-8(x-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11794/selection/b99ad35bc21cc7ff5c845f409a491aeaae3fcca5da41e25f3cd1ce4227077537" :answer/id #uuid "fc491c15-266a-58c7-a2f3-b2b562f21758" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y-1)^{2}=-8(x-4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11794/selection/2c5a32ee0f27351b1ab69d74ef5d4f208f163e9f612055b8c97230813f3a7cbe" :answer/id #uuid "295f8b08-db31-5d74-8c49-7680c33eb4e3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y-4)^{2}=8(x-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11794/selection/9e39ce4346aa0e5949ff4b9f4205d227377ae62a125a163a7b7dac35a190e662" :answer/id #uuid "1da2cb8f-f928-529d-a370-2dbf505caaa9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y-4)^{2}=4(x-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11794/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9eb26fbb-2bef-540d-bb2c-0db2167556de" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-11794/selection/5ea92dcac1f699d65c82b57d915fc42a88835c79e6b904d4ea8c316401c9c0f9" :answer-field/choices ["q-11794/selection/744273781c0ebbac96544b9ea3174f01adea99be43eb05bcf13825a7e5f9db87" "q-11794/selection/5ea92dcac1f699d65c82b57d915fc42a88835c79e6b904d4ea8c316401c9c0f9" "q-11794/selection/b99ad35bc21cc7ff5c845f409a491aeaae3fcca5da41e25f3cd1ce4227077537" "q-11794/selection/2c5a32ee0f27351b1ab69d74ef5d4f208f163e9f612055b8c97230813f3a7cbe" "q-11794/selection/9e39ce4346aa0e5949ff4b9f4205d227377ae62a125a163a7b7dac35a190e662"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-11794" :question/id #uuid "d3122981-1a91-5414-84c6-5eaaa9c218b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-11794" :question/problem "Find the equation of the left-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(1,4)$ and passes through the point $(-1,8).$" :question/worked-solution "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(h,k)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-k)^{2} & =4p(x-h).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the given parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(1,4),$ we substitute $h=1$ and $k=4$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-4)^{2} & =4p(x-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that the given parabola passes through the point $(-1,8),$ so we can substitute $x=-1$ and $y=8$ into the equation above and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-4)^{2} & =4p(x-1) \\\\ (8-4)^{2} & =4p(-1-1) \\\\ 16 & =-8p \\\\ p & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-4)^{2} & =4p(x-1) \\\\ (y-4)^{2} & =4(-2)(x-1) \\\\ (y-4)^{2} & =-8(x-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-11794/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "783ca59b-0242-584c-ae47-004a0eb03817"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11794"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-11800/selection/0ce6e7a33772f2d2c78edb9f87a9748b82efd17ef6011dd1674508eff9e4415f" :answer/id #uuid "5ff4c6d0-5c24-5fcd-9fca-9dfd778178ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+1)^{2}=-(x+4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11800/selection/ddb11cf0f6a52547296a0c13668d67ea96bf795da9c4f7b642ec3d53b7929b77" :answer/id #uuid "be118941-1ee9-5e27-823e-cc3faced7134" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+1)^{2}=-2(x+4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11800/selection/1d4efda05582cb8576f016688eb4982aa1f3a2d404bc626dd5e8b4d1aef1ea36" :answer/id #uuid "2d3da3fb-9648-5131-9c99-e17ca9473916" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+1)^{2}=2(x+4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11800/selection/cc445baceeba34c3e8a5e6fbaf7581c383188227da7bff215f1727c9960e7671" :answer/id #uuid "1ca4baf0-5ed6-5664-b35c-c3a4cfea5285" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+1)^{2}=x+4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11800/selection/577e0e5a6312bfa48ac21aff715f6eea509026ad609ed8dea30267ff34595b42" :answer/id #uuid "97c33400-48bb-59ea-9a6c-72d6af92c00c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+4)^{2}=x+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11800/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c959057f-8262-51b9-9ad1-345ef50afa38" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-11800/selection/cc445baceeba34c3e8a5e6fbaf7581c383188227da7bff215f1727c9960e7671" :answer-field/choices ["q-11800/selection/0ce6e7a33772f2d2c78edb9f87a9748b82efd17ef6011dd1674508eff9e4415f" "q-11800/selection/ddb11cf0f6a52547296a0c13668d67ea96bf795da9c4f7b642ec3d53b7929b77" "q-11800/selection/1d4efda05582cb8576f016688eb4982aa1f3a2d404bc626dd5e8b4d1aef1ea36" "q-11800/selection/cc445baceeba34c3e8a5e6fbaf7581c383188227da7bff215f1727c9960e7671" "q-11800/selection/577e0e5a6312bfa48ac21aff715f6eea509026ad609ed8dea30267ff34595b42"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-11800" :question/id #uuid "c3bdf088-2670-5350-9585-84f5c57baf89" :question/math-academy-id "q-11800" :question/problem "Find the equation of the right-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(-4,-1)$ and passes through the point $(5,2).$" :question/worked-solution "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(h,k)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-k)^{2} & =4p(x-h).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the given parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(-4,-1),$ we substitute $h=-4$ and $k=-1$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+1)^{2} & =4p(x+4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that the given parabola passes through the point $(5,2),$ so we can substitute $x=5$ and $y=2$ into the equation above and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+1)^{2} & =4p(x+4) \\\\ (2+1)^{2} & =4p(5+4) \\\\ 9 & =36p \\\\ p & =\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+1)^{2} & =4p(x+4) \\\\ (y+1)^{2} & =4(\\frac{1}{4})(x+4) \\\\ (y+1)^{2} & =x+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-11800/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "783ca59b-0242-584c-ae47-004a0eb03817"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11800"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115644/selection/3e8158694f254bfc2882eb774fc680f460b1626a27c69b1d89fc59691a3fa1d1" :answer/id #uuid "d6f9e7bd-e468-5b25-9079-86fbab116c49" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+1)^{2}=x-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115644/selection/301fe921b952e085906067be576a7bebe69a61550ce8dc41db541674c3d00cfa" :answer/id #uuid "40be7211-690e-5c55-a5a7-4dab4d23d264" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+1)^{2}=4(x-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115644/selection/89d87167d772a8ba460451200ef08cea08f59961a7623f729c04e702b9b642fa" :answer/id #uuid "9a3e846f-32f6-5f16-8f5e-f61feac1aeb0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y-1)^{2}=-4(x+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115644/selection/055910a123a0ac581abe051c274468eb8ee368447c45813ad817bd3c9554600e" :answer/id #uuid "caf35401-476f-50d5-adfa-3642e0e91ead" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y-1)^{2}=4(x+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115644/selection/ba57991c65a3c15125ea724b9381abca049e4d914b84c3ff206c79df29f02e74" :answer/id #uuid "ca132e3d-7c71-527d-9a9d-4a9bf4df0edb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}=-(y-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115644/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "55868986-7d8f-58a1-895f-439f50031419" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115644/selection/301fe921b952e085906067be576a7bebe69a61550ce8dc41db541674c3d00cfa" :answer-field/choices ["q-115644/selection/3e8158694f254bfc2882eb774fc680f460b1626a27c69b1d89fc59691a3fa1d1" "q-115644/selection/301fe921b952e085906067be576a7bebe69a61550ce8dc41db541674c3d00cfa" "q-115644/selection/89d87167d772a8ba460451200ef08cea08f59961a7623f729c04e702b9b642fa" "q-115644/selection/055910a123a0ac581abe051c274468eb8ee368447c45813ad817bd3c9554600e" "q-115644/selection/ba57991c65a3c15125ea724b9381abca049e4d914b84c3ff206c79df29f02e74"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115644" :question/id #uuid "25ecddc6-e3d2-533f-a083-0601d1ae3713" :question/math-academy-id "q-115644" :question/problem "Find the equation of the right-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(1,-1)$ and passes through the point $(2,1).$" :question/worked-solution "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(h,k)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-k)^{2} & =4p(x-h).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the given parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(1,-1),$ we substitute $h=1$ and $k=-1$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+1)^{2} & =4p(x-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that the given parabola passes through the point $(2,1),$ so we can substitute $x=2$ and $y=1$ into the equation above and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+1)^{2} & =4p(x-1) \\\\ (1+1)^{2} & =4p(2-1) \\\\ 4 & =4p \\\\ p & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+1)^{2} & =4p(x-1) \\\\ (y+1)^{2} & =4(1)(x-1) \\\\ (y+1)^{2} & =4(x-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-115644/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "783ca59b-0242-584c-ae47-004a0eb03817"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115644"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-115651/selection/1576c7c38cfb3d9d775ea6bbdd40a02b9b7db301031743cac1fdcbc7f0aa8e52" :answer/id #uuid "7e3e06d9-c495-5903-aa57-d1a15bd490d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y-2)^{2}=-16(x+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115651/selection/56aad90b11cc111ef9b373b157896b94e227238ff8fa83d3c597f33066a2c203" :answer/id #uuid "a8479efe-2d2b-593b-9941-8faa00a59ce6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+2)^{2}=-4(x-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115651/selection/1c8a0a9596aa926e9465eef82988416328496e5c5ed2f6ce26a9aa8ff9333bd5" :answer/id #uuid "f813091e-61cf-58f4-8d20-f4b493c0c370" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}=-16(y+2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115651/selection/af46e52be053a8bce99eb5921943ed49b3f10ad49596e509e8edf3a40a037d21" :answer/id #uuid "28165a81-f782-5c55-be03-9b15e4b91edf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+2)^{2}=\\frac{16}{7}(x-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115651/selection/e0fc41fdcf4069b25589e50d064bca34d9d44aa1fd218dd6dcbbb76396f30f3c" :answer/id #uuid "3214b975-1a80-5f33-ac6c-8cce8c08dc37" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y-2)^{2}=\\frac{4}{7}(x+1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-115651/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "71adc7bd-0a4e-5816-a972-a31624ec4b98" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-115651/selection/1576c7c38cfb3d9d775ea6bbdd40a02b9b7db301031743cac1fdcbc7f0aa8e52" :answer-field/choices ["q-115651/selection/1576c7c38cfb3d9d775ea6bbdd40a02b9b7db301031743cac1fdcbc7f0aa8e52" "q-115651/selection/56aad90b11cc111ef9b373b157896b94e227238ff8fa83d3c597f33066a2c203" "q-115651/selection/1c8a0a9596aa926e9465eef82988416328496e5c5ed2f6ce26a9aa8ff9333bd5" "q-115651/selection/af46e52be053a8bce99eb5921943ed49b3f10ad49596e509e8edf3a40a037d21" "q-115651/selection/e0fc41fdcf4069b25589e50d064bca34d9d44aa1fd218dd6dcbbb76396f30f3c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-115651" :question/id #uuid "af5ef3a3-53b1-5b4c-810a-f0ac22316bf1" :question/math-academy-id "q-115651" :question/problem "Find the equation of the left-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(-1,2)$ and passes through the point $(-2,6).$" :question/worked-solution "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(h,k)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-k)^{2} & =4p(x-h).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the given parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(-1,2),$ we substitute $h=-1$ and $k=2$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-2)^{2} & =4p(x+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that the given parabola passes through the point $(-2,6),$ so we can substitute $x=-2$ and $y=6$ into the equation above and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-2)^{2} & =4p(x+1) \\\\ (6-2)^{2} & =4p(-2+1) \\\\ 16 & =-4p \\\\ p & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-2)^{2} & =4p(x+1) \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =4(-4)(x+1) \\\\ (y-2)^{2} & =-16(x+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-115651/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "783ca59b-0242-584c-ae47-004a0eb03817"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-115651"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-11806/selection/e3c9c4d543cb23ce22e243c5c959709b99c26b1bf99147fe8772860ff81d5a51" :answer/id #uuid "c5a9327a-6de3-5a92-b644-158c8315aa53" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y-4)^{2}=-3(x+3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11806/selection/b41be047078703ee899ac6d9255004e815907af4387a2f825fedbd443561dd92" :answer/id #uuid "23a2e03b-cd8c-5503-990d-bf4b534d9dd6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+3)^{2}=-2(x-4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11806/selection/665f665c16f852ce359e876bfbf8cf97d11499bb23a20c72ac8295558c0eb53a" :answer/id #uuid "9f283af9-c769-59e5-89b4-5d0b8e4025e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+3)^{2}=3(x-4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11806/selection/5f4fc22b6803e0b394f38fdcb3d751bcb00befbd92cbcce657dd62e2f81ab44f" :answer/id #uuid "f47546f0-680d-5f07-af34-971f7cc9e728" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+3)^{2}=-3(x-4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11806/selection/0152d7ef8ef301b618958fb52093dacc4efd9ab8d26faa1049ccdb292d77f119" :answer/id #uuid "c76cf24a-cb45-502d-bee7-9790cb2a8210" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(y+3)^{2}=2(x-4)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-11806/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "92a37ab3-15d7-534d-8498-4f178dbc8414" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-11806/selection/5f4fc22b6803e0b394f38fdcb3d751bcb00befbd92cbcce657dd62e2f81ab44f" :answer-field/choices ["q-11806/selection/e3c9c4d543cb23ce22e243c5c959709b99c26b1bf99147fe8772860ff81d5a51" "q-11806/selection/b41be047078703ee899ac6d9255004e815907af4387a2f825fedbd443561dd92" "q-11806/selection/665f665c16f852ce359e876bfbf8cf97d11499bb23a20c72ac8295558c0eb53a" "q-11806/selection/5f4fc22b6803e0b394f38fdcb3d751bcb00befbd92cbcce657dd62e2f81ab44f" "q-11806/selection/0152d7ef8ef301b618958fb52093dacc4efd9ab8d26faa1049ccdb292d77f119"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-11806" :question/id #uuid "b87f57ef-1931-500e-98ed-5c572750a3ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-11806" :question/problem "Find the equation of the left-opening parabola that has its vertex at $(4,-3)$ and passes through the point $(1,0).$" :question/worked-solution "The general standard equation of a parabola whose vertex is $(h,k)$ and whose arms open right or left is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y-k)^{2} & =4p(x-h).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we know that the given parabola has its vertex at $(h,k)=(4,-3),$ we substitute $h=4$ and $k=-3$ into the equation above and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+3)^{2} & =4p(x-4).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also know that the given parabola passes through the point $(1,0),$ so we can substitute $x=1$ and $y=0$ into the equation above and solve for $p:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+3)^{2} & =4p(x-4) \\\\ (0+3)^{2} & =4p(1-4) \\\\ 9 & =-12p \\\\ p & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the equation of the parabola is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(y+3)^{2} & =4p(x-4) \\\\ (y+3)^{2} & =4(-\\frac{3}{4})(x-4) \\\\ (y+3)^{2} & =-3(x-4).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-11806/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "783ca59b-0242-584c-ae47-004a0eb03817"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-11806"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
